# C8 anion addition: H-bonded PS rotamer, DIHEDRAL scan about C128-O130.
#
# Goal: rotate the O-O-H about the newly-formed C128-O130 bond to bring H132
# round to O129 and form the five-membered O129...H132-O131-O130-C128 H-bond
# that ps_anion/ lacks (H132...O129 = 3.845 A), the reason PS is +129 kJ/mol
# above RS.
#
# WHY NOT "D 129 128 130 131": that torsion is DEGENERATE. O129-C128-O130 is
# near-planar (the O129=C128 conjugation; angle 102 deg, torsion -4 deg), so
# ORCA's redundant-internal-coordinate generator does not retain it and the job
# dies with "GSTEP: could not impose initial constraints" before step 1.
# (ps_rotamer_scan2/ is that failure on record.)
#
# ANY other substituent of C128 defines the SAME C128-O130 rotation. C120 is
# 55 deg out of the O129-C128-O130 plane, so D 120 128 130 131 is well
# conditioned. Reference substituents of C128: O129 (1.336), O130 (1.507),
# C120 (1.524), C124 (1.527); C124 is the equivalent alternative.
#
# Start at the seed's OWN value (-124.3 deg) so step 1 is the unperturbed
# minimum; MaxIter 500. NO Calc_Hess (scan Hessian bug, 2026-09-25).
# Charge convention: QM region charge on the *xyzfile line; Charge_total = whole
# system. QM -1, host 0, total -1.
! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) Opt TightOpt TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{55 58 61 64 120 121 122 123 124 125 126 127 128 129 130 131 132}
END
Charge_total -1
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
  Scan
    D 120 128 130 131 = -124, 236, 24
  end
  MaxIter 500
end

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
  nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile -1 1 job.xyz
